			"Message": "docs: improve LandFixTier.rs module header",
			"SHA": "957f84e8bf064fe68b3f05c6cdeca1e1848fa23f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T16:13:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				774,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Streamline extension path and NodeResolver module docs\n\nSimplify comments in ScanPathConfigure for extension skip flags and builtin path override to be more concise while preserving the technical details.\n\nCondense the NodeResolver module docstring from verbose prose to a compact ladder list showing the resolution order: LAND_NODE_BINARY → shipped runtime → fnm/volta/asdf/nvm → homebrew → PATH. The resolution behavior is unchanged, only the documentation format is improved for scannability.",
			"SHA": "bcc45254e06f84f91d17cb58716d12de486805f9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T16:03:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				774,
				12
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add extension metadata passthrough, IPC round-trip, and Node version checking\n\nThree major improvements for extension handling and IPC reliability:\n\n1. **Extension manifest passthrough (Atom TH1):** Add 14 new fields to ExtensionDescriptionStateDTO for VS Code package.json metadata: Categories, DisplayName, Description, Keywords, Repository, Bugs, Homepage, License, Icon, AiKey, ExtensionKind, Capabilities, ExtensionDependencies, ExtensionPack. Wind's Extensions sidebar filter `@builtin category:themes` now works — previously categories were absent so the filter never matched.\n\n2. **IPC round-trip for applyEdit/showTextDocument (Atom T1):** Replace fire-and-forget event emission with request/response pattern using SendUserInterfaceRequest. Extensions awaiting workspace.applyEdit() now block until Sky actually applies the edit, fixing races with listeners expecting post-apply state. Also made SendUserInterfaceRequest pub(crate) so Track effect creators reuse the same pattern.\n\n3. **Node version checking (Atom N1):** ResolveNodeBinary now queries `node --version` and logs the resolved version. Emits a warning when major version falls below LAND_NODE_MIN_MAJOR (default 20). Helps diagnose extension host boot failures.\n\n4. **Compile-time PostHog config (Atom P2):** PostHogPlugin now reads API key/host/enable flag from env! baked in build.rs via PropagatePostHogSentinel(). Supports LAND_POSTHOG_DISTINCT_ID for CI correlation. Combined with debug_assertions gate for cheaper no-op path.\n\n5. **IPC logging improvement (Atom I13):** Add paired entry/exit lines per invoke. `done: <cmd> ok=... t_ns=...` on the way out enables latency diagnosis via single grep without Jaeger hopping.",
			"SHA": "f24e444f42f611f00e844728138c5036e8f28793"
		}
	],
